<</Alt(Fig. 4. Trace element abundances of Teg 001, Martian meteorite falls and ALH 84001. Elemental abundances of \(A\) rare earth elements and \(B\) other trace elements, in decreasing order of their tendency to remain in the melt during crystallization. All measurements have been normalized to CI chondrites . Missing values were below the detection limit or not analyzed in previous studies. Red stars connected by thin black lines are two different analyses for Teg 001 . Gray lines are theoretical calculations for partial melting of garnet lherzolite, starting from bulk silicate Mars composition; each line shows a different degree of partial melting, labelled in percent . Colored lines show other Martian meteorites : the depleted shergottite Tissint \(green\); the enriched shergottites Shergotty and Zagami \(both pink\); the nakhlite Nakhla \(thick purple\); the chassignite Chassigny \(thin lilac\); and ALH 84001 \(cyan\). Expand for more)/K 21/P 706 0 R /Pg 112 0 R /S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
